# Manus API (Runtime Agent)

Manus is ClearHead's **runtime agentic layer**. It orchestrates the student support workflow: intake summarisation, urgency routing, signposting, and follow-up. Changes here affect what students see and what advice they get.

## Non-negotiable

Before wiring or changing **any** Manus logic, check the current Manus docs:

- Docs index: https://open.manus.ai/docs/llms.txt
- API v2 intro: https://open.manus.ai/docs/v2/introduction
- Agents: https://open.manus.ai/docs/v2/agents-overview
- Tasks: https://open.manus.ai/docs/v2/task.create (and related task endpoints)
- Skills: https://open.manus.ai/docs/v2/skill.list
- Webhooks: https://open.manus.ai/docs/v2/webhooks-overview
- Safety, limits, and auth: read the relevant v2 pages before shipping

Do not implement from memory. The API evolves; verify agents, tasks, skills, webhooks, and limits against current docs.

## ClearHead scope

Manus handles support-check conversation, urgency band assignment, action-plan generation, copy-ready messages, and check-in follow-up — **not** crisis override. Crisis override stays hardcoded in the app with zero Manus involvement.

## Language

All Manus prompts and outputs must follow the language rules in `PRODUCT.md`. Never frame Manus as a therapist or diagnosis tool.
